{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 3, :comments ["<b>Alef, olot</b> — like <b>ve-ulatna</b> (and its injustice): it closes its mouth. In your hearts is the injustice you do. And this psalm is spoken concerning the judges." "<b>Ḥamas yedekhem</b> — the blood of the bribe." "And the meaning of <b>tefalsun</b> — you weigh it out so that a person will not sense the violence you do. And the meaning: you do violence, as though it were balanced."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 58, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:32:08.394864825Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}